gm-method (a static/gh-pages deploy 'shows no updates' AND the work is genuinely pushed): the cause is usually a DEPLOY-BUILD STEP FAILING SILENTLY since some commit -- the site freezes at the last SUCCESSFUL build while every new push's deploy errors (green-history-then-wall-of-red in `gh run list --workflow=<deploy>`). TWO compounding traps seen together: (1) the work was pushed to a FEATURE BRANCH but the deploy workflow triggers only on push:branches[main] -- so first MERGE the branch to the deploy branch (a clean FF if it is an ancestor: `git merge-base --is-ancestor main feature` then reset main to the feature tip; main being ancestor means no content lost even though one main-only commit existed -- verify its content is in feature by grepping the file it touched). (2) the deploy then FAILED on an ASSET-BAKE step after a sibling-SDK MAJOR BUMP changed the bake API: the workflow imported the OLD export name (bakeProgressive) but the new package's ./bake export is a different fn (bakeCluster) with a different output shape -- mirror the RUNTIME bake call (read src/*/ProgressiveBake.js for the exact fn + output path the client probes) rather than guessing. ROOT-CAUSE deeper than the rename: the source asset was a legacy Draco+webp GLB and @gltf-transform/core 4.3/4.4's reader DEREFS A NULL samplerDef in setTextureInfo on it ('Cannot read properties of null (reading setMagFilter)') -- bumping gltf-transform did NOT fix it. The fix when 'we don't use Draco anymore': RE-EXPORT the asset clean -- read it with NodeIO(+draco decoder, stripping texture.sampler refs to dodge the reader bug), dispose the KHR_draco_mesh_compression extension, write uncompressed; verify VERTEX-IDENTICAL (same verts/prims/mats/tex counts) before replacing the committed binary. Then DELETE the stale progressive-cache so the runtime re-bakes from the new asset, and make the deploy bake step NON-FATAL (if-bake-fails: log ::warning:: + ship the plain GLB; ModelPool degrades to the legacy renderer) so an asset bake can never freeze the whole deploy again. WITNESS the fix on the LIVE deployed page (poolEntities>0 = ModelPool engaged on the real asset, not the fallback), not just a green run -- green != live-updated. And consolidate: after merging, delete every stale branch (content all superseded in main; keep main + the deploy-artifact branch only) so future pushes auto-deploy.